WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.240
Speaker 1: You really have to see this to
believe it.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:10.249
The very same Republican congressman who denied
that there was any insurrection on January

00:00:10.249 --> 00:00:17.940
6th has now been caught in pictures showing
him looking panicked and barricading the doors

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:22.790
of the House of Representatives with furniture
to try to stop the insurrectionists who he

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.510
claimed don't exist from coming into the House
of Representatives.

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:30.220
I'm speaking about Republican Congressman
Andrew Clide.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:35.700
Just last week, he said the riot looked like
a, quote, normal tourist visit.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.750
Those are comments for which he was rightly
excoriated.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:39.440
Ridiculous comments.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:45.079
Here is a picture of the same Andrew Clide
who said insurrection.

00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:47.820
No, this is just a tour.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:54.520
Here he is pushing a piece of furniture surrounded
by security guards up against the doors of

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.590
the House of Representatives.

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:58.560
That's a normal tourist visit.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:04.030
Normal tourist visits require members of the
House of Representatives to barricade the

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.290
doors with furniture.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.360
Here is another picture of Cleide.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:12.270
And he looks, I mean to say he looks scared
for his life.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.070
Is not an exaggeration.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:20.450
It doesn't look like a normal congressional
tourist visit to me, this was Clyde's original

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:21.470
comment.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.270
You really have to see it to believe it.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:24.270
Let me be clear.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:25.980
There was no insurrection.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:30.090
And to call it an insurrection, in my opinion,
is a bold faced lie.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:34.900
Watching the TV footage of those who entered
the capital and walked through Statuary Hall

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:39.100
showed people in an orderly fashion staying
between the stanchions and robes, taking videos

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.100
and pictures.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.830
You know, if you didn't know the TV footage
was a video from January the 6th,

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.870
Speaker 2: you would actually think it was
a normal tourist visit.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:50.880
Speaker 1: It was a normal tourist visit.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:59.380
And yet Congressman Andrew Clide holding up
furniture against the door to prevent the

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:02.200
insurrectionists from breaking in.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:07.750
I haven't heard a response from Clide yet
to these pictures being uncovered, but what

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.420
could he possibly say?

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:15.730
Oh, he was trying to pull down the furniture
to let the peaceful visitors in the images

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:22.180
deceptive because he was taking down the barricades,
not putting them up.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:26.239
I can't even imagine what kind of response
there would be here, but that's one of the

00:02:26.239 --> 00:02:28.480
most absurd that I can think of.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.510
Another possibility would be like maybe to
argue semantics.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.460
Yes, they were breaking in.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:34.460
Yes.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:35.660
Some of them were being violent.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:37.020
Yes, they were trespassing.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:40.820
But we can't call it an insurrection because
they didn't really have a plan for how they

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:45.330
would govern if they succeeded in overthrowing
the government and stopping the process of

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:49.950
counting the electoral votes, like in some
literal semantic sense, because they didn't

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:52.880
have a plan for taking over control of the
government.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.220
It's not an insurrection.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:55.349
I don't know.

00:02:55.349 --> 00:02:59.800
But bottom line, this is yet another attempt
to normalize the situation.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:04.670
And what this goes to is that if they can
make us think, if they can make us believe

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:10.319
that what took place was normal and just blown
out of proportion, maybe by the left, maybe

00:03:10.319 --> 00:03:17.030
they were not even real trumpets, as they
love to say, then they and their fellow Republicans

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:22.920
might be off the hook for any wrongdoing in
pushing for that January 6th insurrection

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:26.560
by spending months claiming the election was
stolen.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.599
And that, of course, includes Donald Trump
as well.

00:03:28.599 --> 00:03:34.330
In normal circumstances, by which I mean sometime
in the past, not recently, we might have thrown

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:36.480
these people out of government by now.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:42.360
But Republican victimhood has allowed them
to cry foul, to blame everybody else and to

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:49.730
continue to wreak havoc and do damage in their
Senate and House of Representative jobs and

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:50.730
roles.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:55.890
And case in point, yesterday's story about
Marjorie Taylor Green and her long record

00:03:55.890 --> 00:04:00.580
of harassment of fellow Congresswoman Alexandria
Cacio Cortez.

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:05.110
That type of behavior would get almost anyone
fired from their job.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:07.390
If you treated a coworker in that way.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:14.670
If in my organization, I found out that somebody
did what Marjorie Taylor Green has done to

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:18.959
Alexandria Castillo, Cortez, I would have
to meet with them and I would have to say,

00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:20.589
you can't work here anymore.

00:04:20.589 --> 00:04:21.859
This is it.

00:04:21.859 --> 00:04:23.220
That's not how this works.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:24.220
It's not allowable.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:25.220
We can't have that.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:26.220
It's outrageous.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:30.979
But they have, to some degree successfully
normalized all of the stuff.

00:04:30.979 --> 00:04:36.520
And that has also included obvious lying,
obvious lying has been completely normalized

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:37.520
as well.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:43.050
So, you know, if I could wrap up with something
optimistic or Forward-Looking that is anything

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:50.140
other than than just horrible desperation
for some kind of semblance of normality, I

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:51.419
would.

00:04:51.419 --> 00:04:55.199
But I don't see any appetite from the American
right wing, from the Republican Party, from

00:04:55.199 --> 00:04:59.719
particularly this Trumpy and wing of the Republican
Party to hold any of these people accountable.

00:04:59.719 --> 00:05:04.499
And so the fear is and I think that the last
few months have shown us that it's a well-founded

00:05:04.499 --> 00:05:05.499
fear.

00:05:05.499 --> 00:05:10.889
The fear is they will continue to do this
stuff and attempt to rewrite history, normalize

00:05:10.889 --> 00:05:17.039
absolutely horrendous things well into the
twenty, twenty two election.

00:05:17.039 --> 00:05:21.990
And if Donald Trump gets his way and he gets
to decide who is on the approved list of good,

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:26.979
good boys and bad boys, good girls and bad
girls and who wins in twenty, twenty two,

00:05:26.979 --> 00:05:32.699
not only may Republicans take over the House,
it may be a particularly Trumpy and Republican

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:38.240
wing that takes over the House and it sets
the stage for Trump or maybe if you can imagine

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:40.139
someone even worse in twenty twenty four.

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:42.259
So I don't think this is trivial stuff.

00:05:42.259 --> 00:05:46.870
And I know we started with just the kernel,
which is a guy who was barricading the doors

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:49.710
now claims that really wasn't an insurrection.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:56.669
And it is a form of gaslighting that leads
to a lot of potentially horrible things getting

00:05:56.669 --> 00:05:58.900
into the midterms in the twenty, twenty four
election.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:01.029
So we will continue to follow it.

00:06:01.029 --> 00:06:07.189
And there are others like Clide making similarly
outrageous statements, which maybe we'll talk

00:06:07.189 --> 00:06:08.679
about later this week.

